#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133568 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d893f937-d802-5d27-b91a-b78caee0313e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "0ab996ae-e3a7-5353-87c2-9b2a01f4f808" :question/math-academy-id "e-5538" :question/problem "Given ![](images/ee/eec8345a2a1eb622aafae6890c6548efcd5b595d18334b5bad9e43f8b0fd4534.png) find $\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{50} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133569 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff66eef8-74b6-5553-af34-7da5a8cbbb02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "f2ff1620-28e1-59ba-97ca-c43f3f300fdf" :question/math-academy-id "e-5539" :question/problem "Given the vectors ![](images/c3/c3261bc45f978551da6b9ae98489e4eeceadfb5a4669a703736b3d623ed2c41d.png) and ![](images/40/40f7e2f6c5aaff24c18d65776fbbb62f44effeb921bc6e54a4e4f7ada905e614.png) find the distance $\\text{d}(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y}).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the distance, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1-2)^{2}+(2-0)^{2}+(3-(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133570 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae41d849-9def-540c-8985-8fbeec679991" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "7b7adf29-1653-5de7-915c-80a09f05995a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5540" :question/problem "Normalize the vector ![](images/33/33fcf438acd77616d7f5c6881234f9dcc87136575b741af6af72eee9d4401dfb.png)" :question/worked-solution "To normalize a vector $\\mathbf{x},$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\dfrac{\\mathbf{x}}{\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|}.$ Therefore, to normalize $\\mathbf{x},$ we first calculate $\\|\\mathbf{x}\\|$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $\\mathbf{x}$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-8}{10} \\\\ \\frac{6}{10}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133639 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "837e0fa4-b8d3-59c1-87c7-44317adafaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Constant Out of the Norm"}] :question/id #uuid "86cf381d-8a69-5290-806b-09477c7ff92e" :question/math-academy-id "e-6190" :question/problem "If $\\left\\Vert {- \\dfrac{ \\mathbf{x} }{2} } \\right\\Vert = 5,$ find $\\Vert 3 \\mathbf{x} \\Vert.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n\\Vert k \\mathbf{x} \\Vert= \\vert k \\vert \\cdot \\Vert \\mathbf{x} \\Vert\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $\\Vert x \\Vert$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-\\frac{x}{2}‖ & =5 \\\\ ‖-\\frac{1}{2}x‖ & =5 \\\\ |-\\frac{1}{2}|\\cdot ‖x‖ & =5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ‖x‖ & =5 \\\\ ‖x‖ & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $\\Vert 3 \\mathbf{x} \\Vert \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3x‖ & =3\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =3\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff66eef8-74b6-5553-af34-7da5a8cbbb02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "008faea9-9932-5ea0-a1b6-3854897c7f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269263} {:answer/id #uuid "987004f7-8842-5a33-a733-c34bc6057244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270611} {:answer/id #uuid "9e509abf-c5d7-596f-8481-e8acfb0b83e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270672} {:answer/id #uuid "bd7a4161-0611-524c-bc9a-a0cf7707a898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270939} {:answer/id #uuid "f4c75e10-03eb-5923-a677-d6d077b71c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4c75e10-03eb-5923-a677-d6d077b71c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271414} :answer-field/id #uuid "20686f79-81b8-5179-a87c-9a9d3f996880" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4733134d-7b59-587f-9448-4d0fcee562ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-139963" :question/problem "Given the vectors $x=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, find the distance $\\text{d}(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(10-4)^{2}+(4-(-4))^{2}+(2-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{8}^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff66eef8-74b6-5553-af34-7da5a8cbbb02" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52ea736d-ccab-54c3-9243-d3cb457641b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324650} {:answer/id #uuid "8573cd6c-9d94-5fb6-a107-920ba8c75139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325098} {:answer/id #uuid "ba551564-9e5b-5878-b9d7-12f2e08d15ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{59}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325572} {:answer/id #uuid "c0c88c90-0109-5937-9ab1-262b852a9d38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325629} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a270f0-93c5-57c3-b42b-56b23fbf1cd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba551564-9e5b-5878-b9d7-12f2e08d15ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{59}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325572} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7b24e37-c1c2-530a-b1d4-51347f584d94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326638}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3145cdd1-bfad-508e-85a8-1beae761a298" :question/math-academy-id "q-39243" :question/problem "Given the vectors $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, find the distance $\\text{d}(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1-4)^{2}+(3-(-2))^{2}+(-2-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+25+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{59}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134239 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "837e0fa4-b8d3-59c1-87c7-44317adafaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Constant Out of the Norm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c232a61-f63e-5828-9810-a195a82fabd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131474} {:answer/id #uuid "b74c36f8-cd95-552e-a905-3f256ff506e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131475} {:answer/id #uuid "e69c4f0b-a13e-5c5c-8de1-e4872b915283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131476} {:answer/id #uuid "5318951a-2acd-5fe7-a9f3-ede27a7c3260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131477} {:answer/id #uuid "75f34e24-a146-51f2-87b3-906a73bb05d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131478}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d25c390d-45c9-5df8-85c6-b1a2100